# Construction of a Virtual Reality Learning Environment for Teaching Structural Analysis.

**Authors:** Chou, Chien, Hsu, Hsieh-Lung, Yao, Yu-Seng

## Abstract
Although structural analysis is a fundamental subject in civil engineering, its abstract concepts and the difficulty in visualizing them pose problems for students. This article examines the application of virtual reality (VR) to civil engineering. Describes the design, development, and evaluation of a VR-based learning center for a structural analysis curriculum. Suggests ways to optimize learning. (PEN)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ554206

